<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nagara River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bednur">Nagara</a> is a river of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> that flows about 166 kilometres from the mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gifu">Gifu</a> Prefecture through the city of Gifu to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ise-bay">Ise Bay</a>. In 1556 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saito-dosan">Saito Dosan</a> was killed in battle beside it by the forces of his son Yoshitatsu. The river is famous for its clear water and for the cormorant fishing practised at Gifu for more than 1,300 years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nagara-river.jpg" alt="Nagara River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Douggers at en.Wikipedia · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nagararivergifu.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
